  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"107\" data-end=\"394\">The <strong data-start=\"111\" data-end=\"129\">Endotoxin test</strong> measures the presence of <strong data-start=\"155\" data-end=\"169\">endotoxins</strong>, which are <strong data-start=\"181\" data-end=\"220\">lipopolysaccharide (LPS) components</strong> found in the outer membrane of <strong data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"278\">Gram-negative bacteria</strong>. These substances are potent triggers of the immune response and are primarily evaluated in the following contexts:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"753\">\n<li data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"502\">\n<p data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"502\"><strong data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"435\">Detecting bacterial contamination</strong> in pharmaceutical products, intravenous fluids, or medical devices</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"576\">\n<p data-start=\"505\" data-end=\"576\"><strong data-start=\"505\" data-end=\"542\">Monitoring bloodstream infections</strong> (especially Gram-negative sepsis)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"577\" data-end=\"658\">\n<p data-start=\"579\" data-end=\"658\">Assessing <strong data-start=\"589\" data-end=\"612\">pyrogenic reactions</strong> in clinical settings or sterile manufacturing</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"753\">\n<p data-start=\"661\" data-end=\"753\">Used in <strong data-start=\"669\" data-end=\"685\">hemodialysis</strong> patients to check for endotoxin contamination in water or dialysate</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"755\" data-end=\"896\">Endotoxins can induce <strong data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"836\">fever, inflammation, hypotension, and even septic shock</strong> if present in the bloodstream or sterile areas of the body.</p>\n<p data-start=\"755\" data-end=\"896\">Elevated Levels : Clinical Implications</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Explanation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gram-negative bacterial sepsis</strong></td>\n<td>Endotoxins released during bacteremia or infection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Contaminated medical fluids/devices</strong></td>\n<td>May introduce endotoxins into sterile body sites, causing febrile reactions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hemodialysis contamination</strong></td>\n<td>Inadequate filtration may allow endotoxin exposure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Systemic inflammatory response syndrome (SIRS)</strong></td>\n<td>Triggered by endotoxemia</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"755\" data-end=\"896\">&nbsp;</p>",
